        "num",
        {
          "min": 0,
          "max": 1000000,
          "step": 1,
          "ph": "10"
        }
      ],
      [
        "d",
        "Não expostos <strong>sem</strong> o desfecho (d)",
        "num",
        {
          "min": 0,
          "max": 1000000,
          "step": 1,
          "ph": "90"
        }
      ]
    ],
    "formula": "<p><strong>RR</strong> = [a/(a+b)] / [c/(c+d)], com EP(ln RR) = √(1/a − 1/(a+b) + 1/c − 1/(c+d)) (Katz, 1978).</p><p><strong>OR</strong> = (a × d) / (b × c), com EP(ln OR) = √(1/a + 1/b + 1/c + 1/d) (Woolf, 1955).</p><p>IC 95% = exp(ln medida ± 1,96 × EP). Com alguma casela zero, soma-se 0,5 a todas (correção de Haldane).</p>",
    "sources": [
      [
        "Katz D, Baptista J, Azen SP, Pike MC. Obtaining confidence intervals for the risk ratio in cohort studies. Biometrics, 1978.",
